 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Concavity:** Standard convex hull algorithms fail on concave objects. This method mitigates this by local convexity classification, but if the classification fails (e.g., due to noisy silhouettes), concave regions may be incorrectly filled [S1].
-*   **Dangling Edges:** If the surface is not closed, edges may be traversed only once. The premise requires each edge to be traversed twice to ensure the surface covers the object tightly without holes [S1].
+*   **Concavity:** Standard convex hull algorithms fail on concave objects [S1]. This method mitigates this by local convexity classification, but if the classification fails (e.g., due to noisy silhouettes), concave regions may be incorrectly filled [S1].
