 ## Background
-The method was proposed to address the limitations of 3D Delaunay Triangulation (DT) and Constrained Delaunay Triangulation (CDT), which are designed for convex shapes and struggle with concavity [S1]. It builds on [Marching Cubes Lookup and Configuration](2518-marching-cubes-lookup-and-configuration.md) by using MC to generate an initial surface, which is then refined using local convex hulls [Parent principle]. The approach was introduced in a paper by [S1] in 2008, aiming to combine the tight fitting of hull methods with the concavity handling of local classification [S1].
